# File headers

Give every new or edited C, C++, or assembly file this block. Keep each original copyright line and each original programmer name. Add `Copyright 2026 Ryan Wilson <ryan@verosnt.com>` under the last copyright line. Add `Ryan Wilson` under `PROGRAMMERS` when the change alters logic.

A file that is entirely new names only Ryan Wilson, with `PROJECT` `VerOS NT Kernel` for `ntoskrnl/`, `hal/`, `boot/`, and `drivers/`; `VerOS NT Subsystem` for `win32ss/`; `VerOS NT System Libraries` for `dll/`; and `VerOS NT` elsewhere. `FILE` is the path from the source root. `PURPOSE` stays one line. A longer note that says what the file does stays in a comment under the header. Keep an `UPDATE HISTORY` block when it records an event. Drop an empty one.

The `LICENSE` line carries the SPDX identifier, so do not add a second `SPDX-License-Identifier` line.

New kernel, driver, boot, and other non-DLL files use `GNU General Public License, version 2 or later (GPL-2.0-or-later)`. New userland DLLs (`dll/` and `win32ss/user/user32*`) use `GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later (LGPL-2.1-or-later)`. On an existing file, keep its license family and fold the notice into that one `LICENSE` line. Do not invent a ReactOS Team copyright the file does not already state.

Leave a public-domain file on its own terms and add `Ryan Wilson` under its contributors. Leave a Wine LGPL header in place and add the copyright line under the existing notice. Do not reformat files listed in `media/doc/WINESYNC.txt` beyond that copyright line.

New PowerShell uses the same six fields as `#` comments. JSON, logs, fixtures, images, `.rc`, and `.inf` do not get this block.

```c
/*
 * PROJECT:     VerOS NT Kernel
 * LICENSE:     GNU General Public License, version 2 or later (GPL-2.0-or-later)
 * FILE:        ntoskrnl/ps/wrkfactory.c
 * PURPOSE:     NT 10.0 Worker Factory Subsystem
 * COPYRIGHT:   Copyright 2026 Ryan Wilson <ryan@verosnt.com>
 * PROGRAMMERS: Ryan Wilson
 */
```

